From a64ac736308fcfd782b0a795c1ceff9abdc17c63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zak Wilson <zak.wilson@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:39:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cheader: a later declarator keeps the base type

struct CallInfo *previous, *next; gave 'next' a bare ptr, so
((ci 'next) 'previous) was refused. The declarator-list support
assumed the first declarator's stars consumed the base, which held
before typed C pointers; c-ptr-to keeps the pointee now, so c-ptr-base
peels the first declarator's levels and each later declarator applies
its own stars to that base. int *p, q; and typedef int *a, b; are
exact instead of refused. Found by the nuc-lua port (its ISSUE-040).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CsC8i2S7yJAHSpzRaddMj3
